| Feature | Why It Matters |
|---------|----------------|
| **Fixed Stack Buffer** | `65_536` bytes lives on the stack. No heap allocation. The garbage collector/allocator is never involved during I/O. |
| **`Interrupted` Retry Loop** | POSIX `EINTR` handling. If a signal interrupts a read, we don't error out—we just retry the same chunk boundary. Prevents false `EOF` or truncation errors. |
| **Streaming Finalization** | BLAKE3's `Hasher` maintains internal state across updates. Calling `extend_from_slice()` repeatedly feeds it without ever requiring a full file load. |
| **Type-Exact Return** | Returns `[u8; 32]` (32 bytes = 256-bit). Avoids vector allocations or hex strings until report time. |

