### 🔍 Memory & I/O Profile Under Concurrency

| Metric | Behavior | Reason |
|--------|----------|----------------|
| **Stack per task** | ~65 KB buffer + ~500 B hasher state | Still O(1) heap. Zero user-space allocations. |
| **Semaphore queue** | FIFO blocking queue in kernel space | Prevents thread starvation via `blocking_acquire()`. |
| **Disk thrashing** | Capped at `disk_io_cap` active readers | OS readahead/seek limits respected. No I/O saturation. |
| **Thread count** | Managed by Rayon pool (usually `num_cpus`). | Decoupled from disk limits; capped I/O guarantees safety. |

---

### 🎛️ Tuning the Cap (`disk_io_cap`)

| Storage Type | Recommended Cap | Why |
|--------------|-----------------|-----|
| Mechanical HDD | `8 – 16` | Physical seek latency (~5–10ms). >16 causes queue starvation. |
| SATA SSD | `32 – 48` | NVMe controllers handle parallelism, but host-side I/O schedulers bottleneck around this. |
| NVMe/UFS | `64 – 128` | High queue depth native to PCIe 4.0/5.0 or UFS 3.1+. |
| Network FS (NFS/SMB) | `4 – 8` | Server-side locking + protocol overhead dominates. |

